    <string name="instructions_hide">Hide instructions</string>
    <string name="instructions_title">Without the companion: enable the web interface in VLC on the PC</string>
    <string name="instructions_step1">In VLC open Tools → Preferences (Ctrl+P) and choose "Show settings: All" at the bottom left.</string>
    <string name="instructions_step2">Interface → Main interfaces: tick "Web".</string>
    <string name="instructions_step3">Interface → Main interfaces → Lua: set a password in "Lua HTTP → Password". Without a password VLC answers 403.</string>
    <string name="instructions_step4">Save and fully restart VLC. On first start allow vlc.exe in Windows Firewall for private networks.</string>
    <string name="instructions_step5">Find the PC address: run ipconfig in Windows (IPv4 address) or use the PC name.</string>
    <string name="instructions_step6">Enter the address, port 8080 and the password above and press "Test" — nothing changes on the TV, we only read the status.</string>
    <string name="instructions_lua" formatted="false">To see the current track and chapter names without the companion, copy the pages from companion/lua into %APPDATA%\\vlc\\lua\\http (install.ps1) and restart VLC.</string>
    <string name="instructions_companion">With the Windows companion all of this is automatic: the PC is discovered, VLC starts on the TV, and audio device, sleep and Bluetooth become available.</string>

